# Case of the Crimson Pulse. Turn 1: it enters as Bot1's last card in hand, so its enters ability discards nothing and
# still draws two; Bot1 plays those out too, and at the end step, with no cards in hand and the Case not solved, the "To
# solve" ability triggers (CR 719.3a) and resolves: the Case is solved (CR 719.3b). Turn 3: the solved upkeep ability
# triggers (CR 702.169c), discards an empty hand and draws two; Bot1 empties the hand again, but a solved Case's "To
# solve" no longer triggers at the end step. Turn 5: it draws two from an empty hand again; turn 7: it discards the
# three Islands in hand, then draws two.

